docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:8:- [docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md](./TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md)
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:15:This backlog translates the temporal timeline proof plan into thin implementation slices tied to the current complaint-generator architecture.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:17:The goal is not to invent a second chronology system. The repo already has normalized temporal context, relation summaries, consistency summaries, temporal proof diagnostics, and operator-facing timeline review. The next work is to consolidate those seams into a canonical timeline registry and a proof-oriented legal timing pipeline.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:22:2. Preserve provenance for every temporal fact, relation, issue, and theorem export.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:23:3. Keep claim-type temporal rules explicit rather than burying them in prompts.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:32:- [complaint_phases/intake_case_file.py](../complaint_phases/intake_case_file.py) already builds normalized `temporal_context`, `timeline_relation_summary`, and `timeline_consistency_summary`.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:33:- [mediator/claim_support_hooks.py](../mediator/claim_support_hooks.py) already assembles element-scoped temporal reasoning context and emits `temporal_summary` in reasoning diagnostics.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:34:- [claim_support_review.py](../claim_support_review.py) already rolls temporal fact, relation, issue, warning, and preview data into claim review payloads.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:35:- [mediator/mediator.py](../mediator/mediator.py) already propagates timeline summaries and packet-level temporal proof readiness.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:36:- [templates/claim_support_review.html](../templates/claim_support_review.html), [templates/document.html](../templates/document.html), and [templates/optimization_trace.html](../templates/optimization_trace.html) already expose operator-facing temporal summaries.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:40:- there is no canonical temporal fact registry spanning testimony, parsed documents, web evidence, and authority references
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:41:- legal temporal rule profiles are not yet explicit per claim type
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:43:- temporal contradiction categories and follow-up actions are not yet a stable contract
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:44:- drafting and readiness gates still consume temporal status mostly as summary metrics rather than claim-rule satisfaction results
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:58:| T0 | Canonical temporal registry | Complete | P0 | One durable fact and relation substrate for chronology |
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:59:| T1 | Claim-scoped temporal graph assembly | Validation Required | P0 | Stable partial-order graphs and issue categories per claim |
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:60:| T2 | Legal temporal rule profiles | Validation Required | P0 | Claim-type specific timing rules and blocking windows |
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:73:Create one durable schema for temporal facts, relations, anchors, and issues across all evidence sources.
