docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:33:- [complaint_phases/intake_case_file.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/complaint_phases/intake_case_file.py) `refresh_intake_case_file(...)` now rebuilds `timeline_anchors`, `timeline_relations`, `temporal_fact_registry`, `event_ledger`, `temporal_relation_registry`, and `temporal_issue_registry` from normalized intake facts.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:35:- [intake_status.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/intake_status.py) `build_intake_case_review_summary(...)` now also preserves the full `event_ledger`, `timeline_anchors`, `timeline_relations`, `temporal_fact_registry`, `temporal_relation_registry`, and `temporal_issue_registry`, so downstream consumers no longer need to reconstruct chronology from summaries alone.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:39:- [mediator/mediator.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/mediator/mediator.py) `_summarize_intake_evidence_alignment(...)` and `_build_alignment_evidence_tasks(...)` already propagate chronology refs such as `event_ids`, `temporal_fact_ids`, `temporal_relation_ids`, `timeline_issue_ids`, `temporal_issue_ids`, and `temporal_proof_bundle_id` into Phase 2 task payloads.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:40:- [mediator/mediator.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/mediator/mediator.py) `_build_alignment_evidence_tasks(...)` now also emits `anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds`, so chronology tasks can point at specific missing ordering predicates and evidence lanes instead of only generic temporal weakness.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:41:- [complaint_phases/phase_manager.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/complaint_phases/phase_manager.py) already treats unresolved temporal registry issues and chronology gap tasks as readiness blockers, and its `proof_readiness_score` now applies an explicit chronology penalty instead of relying only on generic support ratios.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:42:- [claim_support_review.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/claim_support_review.py), [document_optimization.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/document_optimization.py), and [document_pipeline.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/document_pipeline.py) now preserve chronology blocker explanations through review, optimization, and exported package or packet payloads via `claim_support_temporal_handoff`, theorem export metadata, and `chronology_blocker_summary`.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:43:- [claim_support_review.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/claim_support_review.py) `_build_claim_support_temporal_handoff_metadata(...)` already aggregates task-level chronology refs, including `timeline_anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds`, into the review boundary.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:45:- [templates/claim_support_review.html](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/templates/claim_support_review.html), [templates/optimization_trace.html](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/templates/optimization_trace.html), and [templates/document.html](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/templates/document.html) now render chronology anchors, missing temporal predicates, and required provenance kinds in operator-facing review and trace surfaces.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:66:- Phase 1 already builds a canonical `event_ledger` plus anchor, relation, and temporal-issue registries inside the intake case file.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:67:- Phase 2 now carries chronology refs, but it still leans on packet-derived `temporal_rule_status`, `temporal_rule_blocking_reasons`, and `temporal_rule_follow_ups` to decide what chronology work exists. The event ledger is available, but it is not yet the authoritative task-generation source.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:69:- Alignment tasks already carry `event_ids`, relation refs, issue refs, `anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds`, but those fields are still largely derived from packet-level temporal proof data and summary builders rather than authored as first-class chronology execution objects at intake time.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:70:- `_apply_intake_answer_to_case_file(...)` already appends chronology-aware canonical facts, and `_author_temporal_case_file_state(...)` rebuilds anchors, relations, temporal facts, and the event ledger, but chronology updates still rely too much on post-answer reconstruction instead of directly authoring stable event, anchor, and relation objects with durable provenance IDs at answer-application time.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:341:### 1A. Derive temporal evidence tasks from event gaps, not only packet status
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:343:The current Phase 2 task builder in [mediator/mediator.py](../mediator/mediator.py) correctly marks chronology-specific work when packet elements carry temporal-rule metadata. The next step is to ground those tasks in the same event ledger created during intake.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:345:Each temporal evidence task should additionally carry:
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:351:- `temporal_proof_objective`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:352:- `missing_temporal_predicates`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:357:- `event_ids`, `temporal_fact_ids`, `temporal_relation_ids`, `timeline_issue_ids`, `temporal_issue_ids`, and `temporal_proof_bundle_id` already flow through `alignment_evidence_tasks`.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:358:- `anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds` now also flow through `alignment_evidence_tasks`, review payloads, theorem export metadata, and operator-facing trace surfaces.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:361:That change lets Phase 2 ask for the exact missing chronology proof, for example "anchor the complaint date", "prove protected activity occurred before termination", or "resolve contradictory notice dates", instead of only reporting that a packet element is temporally weak.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:489:- `alignment_evidence_tasks[].temporal_fact_ids`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:490:- `alignment_evidence_tasks[].temporal_relation_ids`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:493:- `alignment_evidence_tasks[].temporal_issue_ids`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:494:- `alignment_evidence_tasks[].missing_temporal_predicates`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:496:- `alignment_evidence_tasks[].temporal_proof_bundle_id`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:501:- `claim_support_packet_summary.temporal_gap_task_count`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:502:- `claim_support_packet_summary.claim_support_unresolved_temporal_issue_ids`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:526:- completed: make temporal evidence tasks carry `anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds`
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:527:- completed: extend readiness and packet summaries so unresolved temporal issues remain first-class blockers while also pointing at exact blocked chronology counts and IDs
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:529:- completed: preserve chronology task details through theorem export metadata, claim-support temporal handoff payloads, and operator-facing review or trace templates
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:531:- remaining: derive readiness and evidence-completion scoring from authored ledger completeness, not only temporal counts, rule statuses, and blocker strings
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:586:2. enrich `_summarize_intake_evidence_alignment(...)` and `_build_alignment_evidence_tasks(...)` in [mediator/mediator.py](../mediator/mediator.py) so temporal tasks carry `anchor_ids`, `missing_temporal_predicates`, and `required_provenance_kinds` in addition to the event and issue refs already present
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:587:3. extend [mediator/claim_support_hooks.py](../mediator/claim_support_hooks.py) so validation and gaps emit chronology-specific predicate requirements alongside `missing_fact_bundle` and `satisfied_fact_bundle`, rather than stopping at element-level support status plus temporal-rule summaries
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:597:1. In [mediator/mediator.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/mediator/mediator.py), move chronology authoring closer to `_apply_intake_answer_to_case_file(...)` so new answers create or update stable event, anchor, relation, and provenance-link objects before `_author_temporal_case_file_state(...)` performs summary rebuilding.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:599:3. In [complaint_phases/phase_manager.py](/home/barberb/complaint-generator/complaint_phases/phase_manager.py), extend `_build_evidence_packet_summary(...)` so chronology readiness is informed by anchor coverage, missing predicate coverage, and required provenance coverage, not only unresolved issue counts and temporal-rule status strings.
